WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:07.780
.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:08.648
&gt;&gt;&gt; If you've been on

00:00:08.781 --> 00:00:10.082
Microsoft's home pang you may

00:00:10.483 --> 00:00:13.953
have noticed interesting

00:00:14.086 --> 00:00:17.490
headlines from -- there's an

00:00:17.556 --> 00:00:19.759
obituary calling a late NBA

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:20.493
player useless.

00:00:20.493 --> 00:00:21.661
We have been looking into why,

00:00:21.761 --> 00:00:24.630
and a lot of this comes down to

00:00:24.764 --> 00:00:25.965
company decisions on artificial

00:00:26.132 --> 00:00:26.666
intelligence.

00:00:26.832 --> 00:00:27.500
Artificial intelligence is just

00:00:27.566 --> 00:00:28.934
now seeping into everything.

00:00:29.068 --> 00:00:29.535
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:00:29.669 --> 00:00:31.570
&gt;&gt; And causing chaos it seems.

00:00:31.737 --> 00:00:34.073
&gt;&gt; And nowhere else -- nowhere

00:00:34.507 --> 00:00:35.675
more so than Microsoft

00:00:35.775 --> 00:00:36.075
apparently.

00:00:36.509 --> 00:00:38.577
I think a lot of people say

00:00:38.744 --> 00:00:40.146
Microsoft news, but hundreds of

00:00:40.513 --> 00:00:41.514
millions of people get their

00:00:41.547 --> 00:00:42.848
news from Microsoft because if

00:00:42.982 --> 00:00:44.583
you buy a PC, a computer, that's

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:45.885
your home page very often.

00:00:46.052 --> 00:00:47.586
And there's news there.

00:00:47.687 --> 00:00:51.791
Up until 2018, Microsoft had ace

00:00:51.891 --> 00:00:52.658
journalists working for them.

00:00:52.792 --> 00:00:55.061
Now all that work is mostly done

00:00:55.194 --> 00:00:55.695
by A.I.

00:00:55.795 --> 00:00:56.529
Have a look.

00:00:56.529 --> 00:00:57.196
&gt;&gt; Wow.

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.198
&gt;&gt; It felt like I was standing

00:00:59.532 --> 00:01:02.201
in line at the grocery store

00:01:02.535 --> 00:01:04.537
reading a "National enquirer"

00:01:04.537 --> 00:01:05.538
front page.

00:01:05.538 --> 00:01:06.806
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Farris kwar is

00:01:06.906 --> 00:01:08.007
talking about Microsoft's home

00:01:08.107 --> 00:01:10.543
page also known as msn.com.

00:01:10.543 --> 00:01:12.144
Its aim on the top visited news

00:01:12.545 --> 00:01:14.847
websites in the U.S. And around

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:15.815
the world.

00:01:15.915 --> 00:01:17.016
&gt;&gt; It's absolutely huge.

00:01:17.116 --> 00:01:19.018
It's installed on a lot of

00:01:19.118 --> 00:01:20.553
machines that come with windows

00:01:20.619 --> 00:01:22.555
software on it.

00:01:22.555 --> 00:01:23.656
So people sometimes get that as

00:01:25.191 --> 00:01:25.791
a default as their news source.

00:01:25.891 --> 00:01:28.194
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Over the last few

00:01:28.561 --> 00:01:28.894
months bizarre and false stories

00:01:29.061 --> 00:01:31.564
have gone appearing on msn.com.

00:01:31.564 --> 00:01:32.565
False claims that president

00:01:32.565 --> 00:01:33.966
Biden fell asleep during a

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.569
moment of silence after the maui

00:01:36.569 --> 00:01:38.571
wildfire, an obituary that

00:01:38.571 --> 00:01:40.673
called a late NBA player

00:01:40.806 --> 00:01:42.875
useless, and a false story

00:01:43.008 --> 00:01:43.709
claiming a California politician

00:01:43.876 --> 00:01:45.911
had resigned after attacks by

00:01:46.078 --> 00:01:46.579
Elon Musk.

00:01:46.579 --> 00:01:47.713
&gt;&gt; You had to be responsible in

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.783
what you put on the site because

00:01:50.883 --> 00:01:52.585
so many people would read it and

00:01:52.585 --> 00:01:54.286
could be swayed by it.

00:01:54.587 --> 00:01:56.589
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Renn Pfeifer was a

00:01:56.689 --> 00:01:59.759
contracted editor at nsn.com and

00:01:59.925 --> 00:02:00.860
selected stories from news

00:02:01.026 --> 00:02:01.894
outlets to feature on

00:02:02.061 --> 00:02:02.595
Microsoft's site.

00:02:02.595 --> 00:02:04.597
She was one of more than 800

00:02:04.597 --> 00:02:07.066
editors employed by Microsoft as

00:02:07.166 --> 00:02:08.167
of 2018.

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:09.969
&gt;&gt; I was there on and off for

00:02:10.102 --> 00:02:12.004
eight years before I got laid

00:02:12.104 --> 00:02:13.773
off to be replaced by A.I.

00:02:13.939 --> 00:02:15.841
&gt;&gt; Reporter: In 2020, Renn and

00:02:15.975 --> 00:02:16.876
her colleagues were told they

00:02:17.009 --> 00:02:18.677
were losing their jobs.

00:02:18.844 --> 00:02:20.980
CNN obtained a recording of the

00:02:21.147 --> 00:02:22.648
call announcing the layoffs.

00:02:22.782 --> 00:02:23.883
Editors at Microsoft, they were

00:02:24.049 --> 00:02:25.851
told, were being replace bide

00:02:25.985 --> 00:02:26.685
A.I. Automation.

00:02:26.786 --> 00:02:30.623
&gt;&gt; It's full steam ahead for

00:02:30.623 --> 00:02:31.023
automating all of the --

00:02:31.123 --> 00:02:32.691
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Did you ever think

00:02:32.792 --> 00:02:34.093
you'd have a situation where

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:38.631
you'd be replaced by A.I.?

00:02:38.631 --> 00:02:38.664
&gt;&gt; No.

00:02:38.798 --> 00:02:40.900
Not in a million years.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.635
But here we are.

00:02:42.635 --> 00:02:43.803
&gt;&gt; Reporter: MSN has agreements

00:02:43.903 --> 00:02:46.272
with major news organizations

00:02:46.639 --> 00:02:48.007
including CNN that allows it to

00:02:48.174 --> 00:02:51.010
put their reporting on its site.

00:02:51.177 --> 00:02:51.877
Recently fringe right-wing sites

00:02:52.011 --> 00:02:53.646
have been featured prominently

00:02:53.646 --> 00:02:55.848
on its home page, including

00:02:56.015 --> 00:02:59.018
headlines like these attacking

00:02:59.185 --> 00:02:59.652
president Biden.

00:02:59.652 --> 00:03:00.219
&gt;&gt; Seeing what I'm seeing here

00:03:00.653 --> 00:03:02.321
with MSN is just scary to me.

00:03:02.655 --> 00:03:04.190
Like that can translate to

00:03:04.323 --> 00:03:04.690
tangible votes.

00:03:04.824 --> 00:03:07.226
&gt;&gt; Reporter: If they were going

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.028
to have a -- a front page that

00:03:09.195 --> 00:03:11.230
is all about news, then they

00:03:11.664 --> 00:03:12.932
should take that responsibility

00:03:13.098 --> 00:03:15.835
seriously and understand that it

00:03:15.935 --> 00:03:17.336
has implications for society.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.671
&gt;&gt; Reporter: After his computer

00:03:18.671 --> 00:03:21.140
software updated, Farris

00:03:21.273 --> 00:03:23.676
Cowher's default home page

00:03:23.676 --> 00:03:24.043
changed to Microsoft.

00:03:24.176 --> 00:03:25.678
That's when he began to notice

00:03:25.711 --> 00:03:26.679
something strange.

00:03:26.679 --> 00:03:29.682
&gt;&gt; I think Microsoft is a fairly

00:03:29.682 --> 00:03:30.282
trustworthy company.

00:03:30.683 --> 00:03:32.351
I have -- don't think of them as

00:03:32.685 --> 00:03:33.686
political in any way.

00:03:33.686 --> 00:03:35.688
The content that was being

00:03:35.788 --> 00:03:37.690
pushed definitely skewed to the

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:38.991
right.

00:03:39.158 --> 00:03:39.992
&gt;&gt; Bidenomics proved Joe Biden

00:03:40.092 --> 00:03:42.795
is a buffoon from American

00:03:42.895 --> 00:03:43.095
insider.

00:03:43.262 --> 00:03:44.697
Yeah, that would not have been

00:03:44.697 --> 00:03:46.098
there before.

00:03:46.265 --> 00:03:46.899
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Pfeifer says she

00:03:47.066 --> 00:03:48.167
believes this is happening

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.802
because Microsoft replaced

00:03:49.902 --> 00:03:50.870
editors with A.I.

00:03:51.003 --> 00:03:52.705
&gt;&gt; Still appalled that they have

00:03:52.705 --> 00:03:56.709
these website that's seem like

00:03:56.809 --> 00:03:56.976
fronts.

00:03:57.109 --> 00:03:58.911
Like that are not legit news

00:03:59.078 --> 00:03:59.812
sources pumping out this

00:03:59.912 --> 00:04:02.314
information on the home page.

00:04:02.715 --> 00:04:04.717
&gt;&gt; Let's keep A.I. Under the

00:04:04.717 --> 00:04:07.119
control of people.

00:04:07.286 --> 00:04:08.821
It needs to be safe.

00:04:08.988 --> 00:04:10.723
&gt;&gt; Reporter: But Microsoft won't

00:04:10.723 --> 00:04:12.825
say how many people it has in

00:04:12.992 --> 00:04:15.728
control of its news A.I.

00:04:15.728 --> 00:04:17.396
Renn said the editors who worked

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:18.731
on her team who were hired

00:04:18.731 --> 00:04:19.999
through a subcontractor were all

00:04:20.132 --> 00:04:20.733
laid off.

00:04:20.733 --> 00:04:21.867
&gt;&gt; What's the most important

00:04:21.967 --> 00:04:23.903
thing that our society needs to

00:04:24.003 --> 00:04:25.871
know at this point in our

00:04:26.005 --> 00:04:28.807
history where an editor, human,

00:04:28.974 --> 00:04:31.076
can make those determinations

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:33.312
and it really concerns me that

00:04:33.746 --> 00:04:35.114
A.I. Is being used.

00:04:35.214 --> 00:04:37.216
&gt;&gt; Reporter: On Tuesday "The

00:04:37.316 --> 00:04:38.284
guardian" wrote to Microsoft

00:04:38.417 --> 00:04:40.319
president Brad Smith to express

00:04:40.753 --> 00:04:41.921
its concerns about Microsoft's

00:04:42.021 --> 00:04:43.923
use of A.I.

00:04:44.023 --> 00:04:45.124
Microsoft published a story from

00:04:45.291 --> 00:04:47.126
"The guardian" about lily James,

00:04:47.226 --> 00:04:48.928
a 21-year-old who was found dead

00:04:49.094 --> 00:04:50.763
in Sydney, Australia.

00:04:50.763 --> 00:04:52.898
Microsoft then published an

00:04:53.032 --> 00:04:53.766
a.I.-generated poll next to the

00:04:53.832 --> 00:04:55.768
story asking readers what do you

00:04:55.768 --> 00:04:58.304
think is the reason behind the

00:04:58.437 --> 00:04:59.338
woman's death.

00:04:59.772 --> 00:05:01.006
"The guardian " CEO wrote, not

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:03.242
only is this sort of application

00:05:03.342 --> 00:05:04.310
potentially distressing for the

00:05:04.443 --> 00:05:05.945
family of the individual who was

00:05:06.111 --> 00:05:09.148
the subject of the story, it is

00:05:09.315 --> 00:05:11.784
also deeply damaging to "The

00:05:11.784 --> 00:05:13.786
guardian's" hard-won reputation

00:05:13.852 --> 00:05:15.254
for trusted, sensitive

00:05:15.421 --> 00:05:15.788
journalism.

00:05:15.821 --> 00:05:16.789
Microsoft said it launched an

00:05:16.855 --> 00:05:18.357
investigation and shut off its

00:05:18.791 --> 00:05:18.958
A.I. Polling feature.

00:05:19.792 --> 00:05:21.060
A spokesperson told CNN that in

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:24.930
2021 the company shifted to a

00:05:25.064 --> 00:05:26.799
system that picks stories by an

00:05:26.799 --> 00:05:27.466
algorithm and said we are

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:28.133
committed to addressing the

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:29.802
recent issue of low-quality

00:05:29.935 --> 00:05:31.437
articles contributed to the feed

00:05:31.804 --> 00:05:33.072
and are working closely with our

00:05:33.172 --> 00:05:34.974
content partners to identify and

00:05:35.074 --> 00:05:36.442
address issues to ensure they

00:05:36.809 --> 00:05:37.876
are meeting our standards.

00:05:38.043 --> 00:05:39.345
&gt;&gt; Lot of people don't dig deep

00:05:39.478 --> 00:05:41.180
and do their own homework to

00:05:41.347 --> 00:05:42.481
facts check anything or take

00:05:42.815 --> 00:05:43.816
things at face value.

00:05:43.816 --> 00:05:44.984
There's far too much of that.

00:05:45.084 --> 00:05:47.353
So they read this and take it as

00:05:47.486 --> 00:05:49.822
the factual truth.

00:05:49.955 --> 00:05:51.824
&gt;&gt; Reporter: So as you can see

00:05:51.824 --> 00:05:53.425
there, Microsoft did not make a

00:05:53.826 --> 00:05:55.227
person available to speak to us.

00:05:55.361 --> 00:05:56.929
&gt;&gt; Noticed that.

00:05:57.062 --> 00:05:58.330
&gt;&gt; Brad Smith, Microsoft's

00:05:58.464 --> 00:05:59.832
president, really is on the

00:05:59.832 --> 00:06:00.833
lecture circuit around the world

00:06:00.866 --> 00:06:02.835
telling people how they should

00:06:02.835 --> 00:06:04.269
be responsible with A.I.

00:06:04.436 --> 00:06:07.840
But as we can see here,

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:08.841
Microsoft's own A.I. Is messing

00:06:08.974 --> 00:06:10.275
up the news and potentially as

00:06:10.442 --> 00:06:11.243
we go into election year,

00:06:11.377 --> 00:06:13.245
hundreds of millions of people,

00:06:13.379 --> 00:06:13.979
tens of millions of Americans

00:06:14.079 --> 00:06:16.081
still go to this website daily.

00:06:16.181 --> 00:06:17.149
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:06:17.249 --> 00:06:18.884
&gt;&gt; Could potentially play into

00:06:19.018 --> 00:06:19.284
the election.

00:06:19.451 --> 00:06:20.386
&gt;&gt; Not to put a technical term

00:06:20.853 --> 00:06:22.087
on it, but it seems like A.I.

00:06:22.187 --> 00:06:23.088
Generates a lot of crap.

00:06:23.188 --> 00:06:24.390
&gt;&gt; A lot of crap.

00:06:24.857 --> 00:06:25.858
Hopefully our jobs are safe for

00:06:25.991 --> 00:06:26.859
a while.

00:06:26.859 --> 00:06:27.893
&gt;&gt; A while longer.

00:06:27.993 --> 00:06:29.862
&gt;&gt; A.I.'s not replacing all the

